    {
      "id": "c2cbffa4-b913-4273-8ac3-1705b8b98cc6",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -176,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 672,
        "height": 736,
        "content": "## Sourcing Priority Workflow\nThis workflow is like a smart helper for our buying team. It scores and sorts our projects so we know what to work on first, saving us time and AI credits.\n\n### How it Works\n1. **Get Data:** Pulls new projects from Notion every Monday.\n2. **Score It:** Gives a number score to each project using its cost, urgency, and risk.\n3. **AI Split:** High scores (>20) get an AI summary from Groq. Low scores skip AI to save credits.\n4. **Update:** Sorts the list from highest to lowest score and saves the results in Notion.\n5. **Alerts:** Sends a team update to Slack. If a project is super risky (>50), it also sends a warning email.\n\n### Setup Steps\n1. **Notion Columns:** Make sure your table has: Value, Urgency, Risk, Impact, Effort, AI Rationale, and Priority Score.\n2. **Logins:** Connect your Notion, Groq, Slack, and Gmail accounts in n8n.\n3. **Check Rules:** Set your cutoff numbers in the Switch node (20) and IF node (50).\n4. **Start:** Turn the workflow to \"Active\" to let it run!"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
